  iter-71 EMERGENCY FIX: Adaptive-icon for the DEV (debug) variant.

  Background: @color/ic_launcher_background_dev (pure green #FF00FF00) —
              provides immediate visual distinction from the production build
              on the launcher grid. Mandated by iter-59.
  Foreground: @drawable/ic_launcher_foreground_dev — same "Y" vector glyph
              as the release variant, in white, contrasting against green.
  Monochrome: same drawable — Android 13+ system-tinted single-color layer.

  Root cause that this fixes (iter-71 postmortem): same as release variant —
  @mipmap/ic_launcher (PNG) was used as foreground, violating the adaptive-icon
  spec which requires a drawable layer that can be scaled by the system.
-->
<adaptive-icon xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <background android:drawable="@color/ic_launcher_background_dev"/>
    <foreground android:drawable="@drawable/ic_launcher_foreground_dev"/>
    <monochrome android:drawable="@drawable/ic_launcher_foreground_dev"/>
</adaptive-icon>
